---
// No imports needed — heading is inline since it's inside the card block
---

<section id="photography" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 md:py-32">
  <div
    data-reveal
    class="flex flex-col items-center rounded-2xl bg-muted/50 px-8 py-16 text-center"
  >
    <!-- Camera icon (inline SVG) -->
    <svg
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="40"
      height="40"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.5"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      class="mb-6 text-primary"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path
        d="M2 9.5C2 7.01472 2 5.77208 2.76863 4.94655C3.53726 4.12103 4.77709 4.00873 7.25675 3.78412C8.26399 3.69376 9.06819 3 10 3H14C14.9318 3 15.736 3.69376 16.7433 3.78412C19.2229 4.00873 20.4627 4.12103 21.2314 4.94655C22 5.77208 22 7.01472 22 9.5V15C22 17.8284 22 19.2426 21.1213 20.1213C20.2426 21 18.8284 21 16 21H8C5.17157 21 3.75736 21 2.87868 20.1213C2 19.2426 2 17.8284 2 15V9.5Z"
      ></path>
      <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle>
    </svg>

    <div class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Photography</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        When I'm not coding, I'm behind a camera — landscapes, portraits, and
        anything that catches the light right.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a
      href="/photography"
      class="inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/80"
    >
      View Gallery
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
